<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0"><channel><item><guid>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49766055</guid><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49766055</link><title>Is startpage.com mining Bitcoin when you open it?</title><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:35:21 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;open startpage.com and it will display "verifying your request" and for 30 seconds, it will bump the CPU usage to high on all cores.&lt;p&gt;so what the page doing by using all cpu power just to check what? this is mining behaviour and this started a few weeks ago, since I noticed. other people have noticed it too and said they would not use it anymore because they have to wait +-30 seconds to get some results.&lt;p&gt;did they announce it? could not find anything about that.&lt;p&gt;anyway, I won't use it anymore because 30 seconds of CPU usage is an abuse.&lt;p&gt;not everytime is 30 seconds, it must detect that has used CPU before and sometimes is only a few seconds.&lt;p&gt;I would understand this issue if they put it right on the page "we will do some mining for you to use our service..." or something like that.&lt;p&gt;to reproduce, open first a task monitor where you can check the CPU usage, then open the startpage dot com page and see how the CPU bumps into hyperspace!&lt;p&gt;maybe they are just cleaning the dust on the CPU fan, and that is good for you, right?&lt;/p&gt;
